+# Judiciary mailbox retrospective correction (2026-11-03)
+
+This is an independent judicial fact-finding correction/addendum. It references the exact prior reports and explains which conclusions were unsupported. Original reports are preserved unchanged in `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/judiciary-mailbox/reviewed/`.
+
+## Referenced reports
+- `20261102T183925Z-founder-charter-deployment-blocked.md` (2026-11-02T18:39:25.388741+00:00) — ChatGPT report requesting host-side deployment of 2 Nov evidentiary/blocker-reporting policies to authoritative charter
+- `20261102T193457Z-founder-constitution-correction.md` (2026-11-02T19:34:57.020199+00:00) — Founder clarification withdrawing constitutional deployment; policies are operational, not constitutional; repo constitution reverted to match authoritative 14 Oct 2026
+
+## Findings
+1. The requested "host-side installation of constitution/CONSTITUTION.md at the protected authoritative source" was **withdrawn by the Founder** as an error (policies are operational, not constitutional). The earlier disposition's actionable conclusion demanding host installation is factually superseded. No verified host-side deployment is required for these operational rules.
+2. Repository changes enforcing operational policy (government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md, sitting/branch-health/audit-cycle machinery) are the appropriate channel per Founder clarification. The authoritative Constitution remains the 14 Oct 2026 text (byte-identical per clarification).
+3. The "deployment blocked" framing treated an operational rule as constitutional - that classification was unsupported given the Founder's explicit withdrawal and clarification. The impediment described does not constitute an unresolved defect requiring host charter modification.
+4. The reports remain historically important; their actionable interpretation is corrected here without rewriting the original files.
+
+## Disposition
+- Treat `20261102T183925Z-founder-charter-deployment-blocked.md` as **historical with withdrawn actionable demand** (no open defect to resolve via charter deployment).
+- Enforce the operational reporting/blocker rules via the existing government machinery as directed.
+- No changes to measurement machinery proposed/implemented by Judiciary (per mandate).
+
+Evidence inspected: the two reports above, git history (commits c730633 mentioned in clarification context, current HEAD 753468c), Constitution files in repo and understanding of Founder clarification.
